            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; padding: 12px; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 14px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
<h3>What's New</h3>
<h2>New Features</h2>
<ul>
<li>Settings → Remote Access has a new &quot;Install Addy Mobile&quot; row for joining the Addy Mobile beta on TestFlight. Click &quot;Show QR code&quot; to get a code you can scan with your iPhone, along with step-by-step instructions, or use &quot;Copy link&quot; or &quot;Open in browser&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>The &quot;Pair a phone&quot; section in Remote Access settings now explains that Addy Mobile finds a nearby Mac by itself. The one-time pairing code is now behind &quot;Pair manually&quot;, for when the Mac doesn&#x27;t show up, and the connection status now appears under the &quot;Allow remote access&quot; switch.</li>
<li>When an automatic CLI update keeps failing, Addy now waits longer between attempts instead of retrying every hour. The wait doubles after each failure in a row, up to once a day, and goes back to normal after the next successful update.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Failed automatic CLI updates now show the real reason they failed. Before, updaters that print their error to normal output, such as cursor-agent, showed no useful message, and the cause at the end of long installer logs like npm&#x27;s could be cut off.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
